# Database Patterns (Drizzle + Neon)

## Schema definitions
Always create schemas in `packages/database/src/schema/<name>.ts`:

```typescript
// @ts-nocheck
import { pgTable, text, uuid, timestamp, boolean, integer } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";

export const items = pgTable("items", {
  id: uuid("id").primaryKey().defaultRandom(),
  userId: text("user_id").notNull(),           // Clerk user ID
  orgId: text("org_id"),                        // Clerk org ID (for teams)
  name: text("name").notNull(),
  isPublic: boolean("is_public").default(false),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at").defaultNow().notNull(),
});

export type Item = typeof items.$inferSelect;
export type NewItem = typeof items.$inferInsert;
```

Export from `packages/database/src/schema/index.ts`:
```typescript
export * from "./items";
```

## Queries
```typescript
import { db } from "@launchkit/database";
import { items } from "@launchkit/database/schema";
import { eq, and, desc, ilike } from "drizzle-orm";

// Select
const rows = await db.select().from(items).where(eq(items.userId, userId)).orderBy(desc(items.createdAt));

// Insert + return
const [row] = await db.insert(items).values({ userId, name }).returning();

// Update
await db.update(items).set({ name: "new" }).where(and(eq(items.id, id), eq(items.userId, userId)));

// Delete
await db.delete(items).where(eq(items.id, id));

// Search (case-insensitive)
const results = await db.select().from(items).where(ilike(items.name, `%${query}%`));
```

## Vector/RAG queries (pgvector)
```typescript
import { sql } from "drizzle-orm";

// Cosine similarity search
const similar = await db.execute(sql`
  SELECT id, content, metadata,
    1 - (embedding <=> ${embedding}::vector) AS similarity
  FROM documents
  ORDER BY embedding <=> ${embedding}::vector
  LIMIT ${k}
`);
```

## Apply schema
```bash
pnpm db:push         # Push changes to Neon
pnpm db:studio       # Open Drizzle Studio (browser UI)
pnpm db:generate     # Generate migration files
```

## Multi-tenant pattern
Always scope queries by `userId` OR `orgId` (for team resources):
```typescript
const { userId, orgId } = await auth();
// Personal resource
.where(eq(items.userId, userId))
// Team resource (falls back to personal)
.where(orgId ? eq(items.orgId, orgId) : eq(items.userId, userId))
```
